    {
      "revision": "r03",
      "review": "Root review rejected pumpkin/bulb rows and hard front gold ledge; pale beam strips and uniform ornament hierarchy remained."
    },
    {
      "revision": "r04",
      "repair": "Replaced actual lotus geometry on all three seats. Meridian opens out toward pointed tip rather than a sin-shaped belly returning inward; thin closed concave roots, outward flared edges, returned solid margins and 3 unequal staggered rings. Source-derived support inset10percent and dark under source envelope. Aged structural red timber and separate darker rear framing plus distinct furnishing/gilt roles."
    },
    {
      "revision": "r05",
      "review": "Native material rays confirmed old beam undersides/rear framing but left pale front strips; exact second ray inspection identified those strips as glossy black lacquer beam faceplates, not cream-painted wood. Geometry remains R04."
    },
    {
      "revision": "r06",
      "repair": "Dedicated worn black lacquer on actual beam faceplates/coffer frames removes pale clearcoat bands; underside lacquer remains separate from structural red timber, columns, gold and floor. Actual low-front hero from Y1.05m and lower oblique from Y1.35m replace the eye-level diagnostic as respectful views. Full, low-front and low3q inspected for physical support without source anatomy changes."
    }
  ],
  "r08RepairReason": "Actual R07 image closed upper voids but appeared as a smooth pot with shallow intersecting patchwork. R08 uses a continuous analytic profile without flat-tangent section bands and clearly raised convex solid petal carving with positive front clearance.",
  "r07RepairReason": "Root rejected R06 black upper triangular voids/pointed fan. R07 uses a continuous closed bowl/core lofted to actual3D hem contours, then carves overlapping shallow solid petals on that volume. Actual native low-front/full/oblique images determine visual support, not topology metrics.",
  "currentNativeObservations": [
    "R08 continuous closed concave/convex lobed bowls carry all3 actual XYZ hem contours; R06 independent flat leaf crowns and R07 shallow pot-like relief are superseded. Actual measured XYZ foot contours carry all3 unchanged bodies.",
    "Deeper overlapping convex solid petals follow one smooth analytic bowl profile, with restrained tips and clear relief above the continuous backing, so upper contact areas have a continuous gilt backing rather than black triangular voids.",
    "The main bowl top loft tucks into the actual raw hem contour without an exposed broad flat gold shelf; actual source hem vertices remain unchanged.",
    "R06 worn beam faceplates, deep structural lacquer, subdued furnishing gilt and respectful low cameras remain."
  ],
  "remainingPhotographicDifferences": [
    "The actual source is a different Japanese Amida: smooth fire-damaged scalp, youthful face, shallow U-fold chest and prepared symmetric pose differ from reference. These actual source anatomy surfaces remain unchanged.",
    "R08 bowl and carved petals remain more regular and simplified than the photographed continuous hand-carved lotus; source hem irregularity remains visible.",
    "The still-curated bilateral medial fold seam and raw source hem remain visible close up.",
    "Attendant anatomy, some floral/coffer/openwork patterns, furniture proportions and overall room construction remain different.",
    "Native room cube captures, bounce proxies, GTAO and planar varnish are still approximations; native gold/shadow response remains visibly CG.",
    "A physical Cycles image is a cross-renderer diagnostic with actual GI and its own calibrated exterior boundary/AgX; it is not automatic native/movie replacement or WebGL pixel equivalence."
